Implemented REL-RC-G in [files.py](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/packages/tools/src/disco/tools/builtin/files.py) and added regressions in [test_rel_rc_g_line_recovery.py](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/packages/tools/tests/test_rel_rc_g_line_recovery.py).

What changed:
- `file_replace_lines` / `file_insert_lines` success output now includes updated numbered content windows with total line count and shifted-number guidance.
- Line-edit `STALE_FILE_CONTEXT` / `FRESH_READ_REQUIRED` refusals now carry fresh numbered content: full file up to 16KB, otherwise ±40 lines around the attempted range.
- That refusal content is credited in `reads[path]` without setting `read_since_write`, so corrected line edits can proceed but blind `file_write` remains blocked.
- Same-line-count `file_replace_lines` advances grounding for consecutive line edits without a reread.

